# MARS Agent Rules

## Stack

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (no custom CSS files unless unavoidable)
- Supabase for Auth, Postgres, Storage, RLS
- Deploy on Cloudflare Workers via `@opennextjs/cloudflare` + Wrangler (not Vercel)
- Domain/DNS on Cloudflare; email MX on Google Workspace

## Security

- Enforce Supabase RLS on every public table
- Never expose `author_id` on reviews to browser/public clients — use `public_reviews` (or equivalent DTO) without that column
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is server-only; never ship it to the client
- Review authors cannot UPDATE/DELETE their own reviews after insert (RLS)

## Components

- Functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- Keep UI modular: presentational pieces (e.g. ReviewCard) separate from data fetchers (e.g. ReviewFeed)

## Process

- Plan Mode: before sweeping architecture changes, write a step-by-step plan and wait for approval
- Write unit tests for API handlers and aggregation utilities before building the related UI
- Prefer editing existing files; avoid drive-by refactors and unsolicited markdown docs
